{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792248599,"nonce":"NxZc3WxGgoHGYPLQ5/n8NpeRpR0=","title":"Side-module GOT.mem entries for the library's own data omit __memory_base","message":"Reported by ashui-f2 (ashui git-bug 0c8c9a0). A position-independent side module exports each data symbol it defines as a global holding an offset from __memory_base, and reaches it through a GOT.mem import that the loader must fill with the absolute address. Both loaders (native/dylink.rs and browser/dylink.rs, data_address) filled it with the exported global's raw value, so every static the module reached through GOT.mem pointed into the program's memory instead of its own data. In blinc_abi.wasm that made OnceLock state read as initialised with a null vtable and Signal.set trapped 'uninitialized element'. xgpu.wasm and sqlite.wasm only worked because none of their own statics went through GOT.mem.\n\nFix: add the library's memory base for a symbol the library defines; the program's own exports are absolute and unchanged. Test: crates/ash_wasm_runtime/tests/side_module_data.rs (fails before, passes after).","files":null}]}